"comparison": "Both Intel and AMD highlight the integration of Neural Processing Units (NPUs) into their client CPUs to enable AI PC capabilities in 2024. Intel disclosed that it ramped sales of the Intel Core Ultra Series 1, its 'first product with an integrated neural processing unit,' manufacturing it on the Intel 4 process. Similarly, AMD disclosed that it 'was the first company to integrate a dedicated neural processing unit (NPU) on the same SoC as an x86 CPU for AI PCs.' While both companies competed on being first with integrated NPUs for x86 AI PCs, Intel specifically noted the manufacturing node (Intel 4) for this series, whereas AMD's statement emphasized the architectural integration on the SoC as a first-mover claim.",
