"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both companies detailed their 2024 mobile processor releases targeting AI and efficiency. Intel launched the Intel Core Ultra 200V Series, manufactured by an external foundry, which leverages Xe2 GPU architecture for improved efficiency and AI acceleration in thin and light notebooks. AMD released the AMD Ryzen AI 300 Series processors in 2024, featuring an NPU and its latest 'Zen 5' architecture. Both disclosures focus on the specific 2024 product lines that incorporated NPU technology and next-generation architectures (Intel's Xe2/AI acceleration vs. AMD's Zen 5) to address the AI PC market.",
